{
  "manufacturer": "Kohler",
  "manufacturer_slug": "kohler",
  "model": "Decision-Maker 6000 generator set controller",
  "model_slug": "decision-maker-6000",
  "short_model": "DM6000",
  "aliases": [
    "Decision-Maker 6000",
    "DEC 6000",
    "Kohler 6000 controller"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Generator controller",
  "applies_to": "Kohler Decision-Maker 6000 generator set controllers, Modbus RTU on the controller's RS-485/RS-232 port, per section 8 of TP-6113.",
  "summary": "The Decision-Maker 6000 is a Kohler generator set controller whose Modbus map follows the same layout as the Decision-Maker 550. It answers Modbus RTU directly with a holding-register map of generator electrical output, engine status from the ECM or local senders, run-time and maintenance counters, system setpoints, remote timed-run commands and a 16-word system event stack. This map covers the electrical and engine blocks, master switch and mode status, run-time counters, key system settings and the remote functions.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual prints 6-digit holding-register references (400001 = first holding register, 409999 = register 49999 in 5-digit form), so 400001 is wire address 0 and 401306 is wire address 1305."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Communications Protocol Operation (generator set, transfer switch and power monitor controllers)",
    "doc_number": "TP-6113 12/21p",
    "revision_date": "2021-12",
    "url": "https://resources.kohler.com/power/kohler/industrial/pdf/tp6113.pdf",
    "pages": "Serial settings and data types pp. 15-16; function and exception codes p. 17; DM6000 specifications p. 111; register guide p. 114; registers pp. 115-127"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Data types follow the manual's definitions: WORD = 16-bit unsigned, SWORD = 16-bit signed, LONG = 32-bit unsigned with the least significant word first, so LONG registers are listed CDAB.",
    "Oil, fuel and coolant pressures and temperatures follow 400139 Metric Units: kPa and °C when metric, psi and °F otherwise. The units shown assume metric.",
    "Left out: user-calibrated analog inputs 1-7, DDEC-only values, the 2-word date fields (byte-packed day|month), maintenance date/time fields, time-delay and protective setpoints, analog/digital input setup, relay driver definitions, event history, strings and the defined common faults.",
    "Only system event word 1 is listed; the stack runs 401500-401515 (events 0-255) and must be read as one 16-register block."
  ],
